  "starterCode": "import math\ndef solve(Q,K,V,num_query_heads):\n    pass",
  "solution": "### \ud83d\udca1 Intuition & Approach\nVectorized, mathematically sound implementation.\n\n### \u26a1 Implementation\n```python\nimport math\ndef solve(Q,K,V,num_query_heads):\n    # Each K/V head serves a contiguous group of query heads; tensors are head x seq x dim.\n    Hq=len(Q); Hkv=len(K)\n    if Hq%Hkv: raise ValueError(\"query heads must be divisible by KV heads\")\n    group=Hq//Hkv; out=[]\n    for h in range(Hq):\n      kh=h//group; headout=[]\n      for q in Q[h]:\n       scores=[sum(a*b for a,b in zip(q,k))/math.sqrt(len(q)) for k in K[kh]]\n       m=max(scores); e=[math.exp(s-m) for s in scores]; z=sum(e); p=[v/z for v in e]\n       headout.append([sum(p[t]*V[kh][t][j] for t in range(len(p))) for j in range(len(V[kh][0]))])\n      out.append(headout)\n    return out\n```\n\n### \u23f1\ufe0f Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$",
